`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"where-is-claude-live",children:"Where do I see every channel Claude Tag is working in?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"The access editor's left rail (section 4) is the roster: every channel Claude Tag has been added to appears there automatically, whether it has spent anything or not. Spend by channel and per-channel limits live on the Usage page, and the Analytics page shows spend by channel read-only, including promotional-credit usage that the Usage page reports as $0.00 (section 6 also has the reseller note)."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"mention-only",children:"Can I make it mention-only across the whole organization?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Not organization-wide; the switch is per channel. ",(0,n.jsxs)(r.strong,{children:["Turn off ",(0,n.jsx)(r.code,{children:"Respond automatically"})]})," on the channel scope's ",(0,n.jsx)(r.code,{children:"Advanced"})," settings in Admin settings, on the channel's ",(0,n.jsx)(r.code,{children:"Configure"})," page, or just by telling Claude Tag in the channel, and it holds for everyone there; see ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://claude.com/docs/claude-tag/users/when-claude-responds#turn-automatic-replies-on-or-off",children:"controlling when Claude Tag responds"}),'. If you need a hard organization-wide boundary instead, use the enforced controls listed under "The hard boundaries" in section 5.']}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"whose-permissions",children:"Whose permissions does Claude Tag use?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Its own service accounts in channels; the asker's own claude.ai account in direct messages. Where Anthropic has enabled personal connectors in channels, the asker's own connectors can also serve their own request after they allow it, recorded under their name. Section 4 has the identity model."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"block-a-channel",children:"Can I block Claude Tag from a channel before someone invites it?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Yes: ",(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"a Blocked channel pattern"})," (the Advanced settings in section 4) keeps it out of matching channels even if someone invites it, and one channel's own ",(0,n.jsx)(r.code,{children:"Enable Claude Tag in this channel"})," switch does the same for that channel. To confine it to chosen channels instead, see ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://claude.com/docs/claude-tag/admins/restrict-access#limit-claude-tag-to-specific-channels",children:"limiting Claude Tag to specific channels"})," in the docs (on a Team plan, blocked channel patterns are the fence)."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"read-or-delete-memory",children:"Can I read or delete what it remembers?"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Yes. An Owner can open a scope's memory files from the scope's menu, and can edit or delete them. Anyone in a channel can also ask Claude Tag what it remembers and tell it to update or forget an entry."}),`
